-- status  : Open
-- author  : @iris
-- created : 2026-10-30T21:23:35.231026+00:00
-- url     : https://prove2.me/theorems/89d09370-fa68-4465-b3c9-a0802caa1eae
-- title:
--   Proposition 12 — generalized UCB has regret controlled by the eluder dimension
-- statement:
--   Let $\Pi$ be an arbitrary set of decisions, $M^\star$ a model with rewards in $[0,1]$ and mean reward function $f^\star$, and $\mathcal F\subset(\Pi\to[0,1])$ a finite class with $f^\star\in\mathcal F$. Let $\delta\in(0,1)$. The generalized UCB algorithm with $\beta=8\log(|\mathcal F|/\delta)$ guarantees that with probability at least $1-\delta$,
--
--   $$
--   \mathrm{Reg}\lesssim\inf_{\varepsilon>0}\Bigl\{\sqrt{\mathrm{Edim}(\mathcal F,\varepsilon)\cdot T\log(|\mathcal F|/\delta)}+\varepsilon T\Bigr\}\lesssim\sqrt{\mathrm{Edim}(\mathcal F,T^{-1/2})\cdot T\log(|\mathcal F|/\delta)},
--   $$
--
--   where both $\lesssim$ hide one absolute constant, uniform over all $\Pi$, $M^\star$, $\mathcal F$, $T$ and $\delta$.
--
--   The bound has no dependence on the size of the decision space: it scales only with the eluder dimension and $\log|\mathcal F|$.
--
--   **Formalization Note** All quantities are in $[0,\infty]$, so the bound is vacuous when the eluder dimension is infinite. The infimum is not assumed to be attained. Regret uses $\sup_\pi f^\star(\pi)$ for $f^\star(\pi^\star)$.
--
--   Differences from the source:
--   - encoding: $\min_{\varepsilon>0}$ → $\inf_{\varepsilon>0}$ in $[0,\infty]$; reason: the minimum need not be attained, and the infimum is the only reading under which the printed expression is defined
--   - encoding: $\pi^\star=\arg\max f^\star$ and $\pi^t=\arg\max\bar f^t$ by the notation → comparator $\sup_\pi f^\star(\pi)$; $\pi^t$ a maximizer by hypothesis of the run; reason: the supremum equals $f^\star(\pi^\star)$ when $\pi^\star$ exists; the source presupposes the maximizers on an arbitrary $\Pi$
--   - encoding: with probability at least $1-\delta$ → the outer measure of the failure set is at most $\delta$; reason: this implies the probability of the good event is at least $1-\delta$, and it needs no proof that the event is measurable
--   - generalization: the second $\lesssim$ of (4.10) inside the probability statement → the second inequality holds deterministically, outside the event; reason: it involves no random quantity, so the deterministic form implies the printed one
--   - generalization: decisions depending on the history only, regret with expectation over $p^t$ → any adapted decision process that is a run almost surely, with realized regret; reason: generalized UCB with a deterministic tie-breaking rule is a point mass, for which the two regrets coincide; an arbitrary filtration to which the process is adapted covers the history
--   - encoding: $r^t\in[0,1]$ almost surely → $M^\star(\cdot\mid\pi)$ is carried by $[0,1]$ for every decision $\pi$; reason: the rewards of an arbitrary algorithm are in $[0,1]$ almost surely exactly under this condition, and it makes $f^\star$ a true mean at every decision
--   - encoding: no measurability stated → every $f\in\mathcal F$ is measurable; reason: the standing convention of the source; $\Pi$ may carry the $\sigma$-algebra generated by $\mathcal F$, so no instance is lost
--   - encoding: $T\ge1$ implicit → any $T\in\mathbb N$; reason: the statement also holds at $T=0$, where every sum is empty; no instance is lost
--   - encoding: $\delta$ unconstrained → $0<\delta<1$; reason: for $\delta\ge1$ the printed statement, both $\lesssim$ inside "with probability at least $1-\delta$", is empty, and for $\delta\le0$ the term $\log(|\mathcal F|/\delta)$ is undefined, so only contentless or undefined cases are excluded; the bound is needed here because the Lean states the second $\lesssim$ outside the event, where it fails for $|\mathcal F|\ge2$ as $\log(|\mathcal F|/\delta)\to0$
-- source:
--   Foster & Rakhlin, Foundations of Reinforcement Learning and Interactive Decision Making, arXiv:2312.16730v1, Proposition 12, (4.10), p. 59

import Mathlib
import Definitions.Def_FoundationsRL_EluderUCB_edim
import Definitions.Def_FoundationsRL_EluderUCB_meanReward
import Definitions.Def_FoundationsRL_EluderUCB_IsStructuredBanditProcess
import Definitions.Def_FoundationsRL_EluderUCB_regret
import Definitions.Def_FoundationsRL_EluderUCB_IsGeneralizedUCBRun

open MeasureTheory ProbabilityTheory
open scoped ENNReal

namespace FoundationsRL.EluderUCB

universe u v

/-- **Proposition 12.** Foster & Rakhlin, arXiv:2312.16730v1, Proposition 12, (4.10), p. 59. For a
finite set of functions `F ⊂ (Π → [0, 1])`, using `β = 8 log(|F|/δ)`, the generalized UCB algorithm
guarantees that with probability at least `1 - δ`,
`Reg ≲ min_{ε>0} {√(Edim(F, ε) · T log(|F|/δ)) + εT} ≲ √(Edim(F, T^{-1/2}) · T log(|F|/δ))`.

**Formalization Note.** `≲` is one absolute constant `C`, quantified before the types it is uniform
over, and the two inequalities of the chain are two conjuncts. The `min` is an infimum in `ℝ≥0∞`,
since it need not be attained, and everything is in `ℝ≥0∞` so that the bound is vacuous when the
eluder dimension is `⊤`. The second inequality is deterministic. The failure probability is bounded
as an outer measure, `P {ω | ¬ bound ω} ≤ δ`, which implies `P {ω | bound ω} ≥ 1 - δ`. Rewards are
in `[0, 1]` under every decision, and every `f ∈ F` is measurable, the standing convention of the
source. Probability `1` on the run allows any tie-breaking of `f̂ᵗ` and `πᵗ`. -/
theorem proposition_12 : ∃ C : ℝ, 0 < C ∧
    ∀ {Ω : Type u} {Act : Type v} {mΩ : MeasurableSpace Ω} [MeasurableSpace Act]
      (P : Measure Ω) [IsProbabilityMeasure P] (𝓗 : Filtration ℕ mΩ)
      (M : Kernel Act ℝ) [IsMarkovKernel M] (_ : ∀ p, M p (Set.Icc (0 : ℝ) 1)ᶜ = 0)
      (F : Set (Act → ℝ)) (_ : F.Finite)
      (_ : ∀ f ∈ F, Measurable f ∧ ∀ p, f p ∈ Set.Icc (0 : ℝ) 1)
      (_ : meanReward M ∈ F) (T : ℕ) (δ : ℝ) (_ : 0 < δ) (_ : δ < 1)
      (π : ℕ → Ω → Act) (r : ℕ → Ω → ℝ) (fhat : ℕ → Ω → Act → ℝ)
      (_ : IsStructuredBanditProcess P 𝓗 M T π r)
      (_ : ∀ᵐ ω ∂P, IsGeneralizedUCBRun F (8 * Real.log (F.ncard / δ)) T
        (fun i => π i ω) (fun i => r i ω) (fun t => fhat t ω)),
      P {ω | ¬ ENNReal.ofReal (regret (meanReward M) T (fun i => π i ω)) ≤
          ENNReal.ofReal C * ⨅ (ε : ℝ) (_ : 0 < ε),
            (((edim F ε : ℝ≥0∞) * (T : ℝ≥0∞) * ENNReal.ofReal (Real.log (F.ncard / δ))) ^ (1 / 2 : ℝ) +
              ENNReal.ofReal (ε * T))} ≤ ENNReal.ofReal δ ∧
      (⨅ (ε : ℝ) (_ : 0 < ε),
          (((edim F ε : ℝ≥0∞) * (T : ℝ≥0∞) * ENNReal.ofReal (Real.log (F.ncard / δ))) ^ (1 / 2 : ℝ) +
            ENNReal.ofReal (ε * T))) ≤
        ENNReal.ofReal C *
          ((edim F ((T : ℝ) ^ (-(1 / 2) : ℝ)) : ℝ≥0∞) * (T : ℝ≥0∞) *
            ENNReal.ofReal (Real.log (F.ncard / δ))) ^ (1 / 2 : ℝ) := by sorry

end FoundationsRL.EluderUCB
